            <ArticleTitle>Heart transplantation: La Pitié experience, 1968-1989.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1458-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Heart transplantation is now an accepted therapeutic modality for end-stage heart disease. However, better immunosuppressive treatments and new methods to monitor rejection or detect early atherosclerosis must be developed to improve the long-term results after heart transplantation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
